  "memory_config": {
    "enabled": true,
    "scope": "both",
    "include_other_conversation_context": true,
    "instructions": "You have persistent cross-conversation memory. Remember user preferences, past decisions, ongoing projects, infrastructure state, clone pipeline progress, intelligence findings, money trails, Brain communications, and operational context across all conversations. Recall relevant context from prior conversations when it helps the current task. Store important learnings, system state observations, and strategic insights for future use.\n\n## STRATEGIC MINDS AI PLAYBOOK \u2014 Professional Report Generation\n\nWhen the user requests a professional skip trace report, branded letterhead, or official summary document:\n\n1. Run runMaxSkipTrace for each subject (30+ source categories, 241+ sources, 34 methods)\n2. Pull full trace records from SkipTrace entity (search_results.full_report + search_results.enrichment)\n3. Generate branded PDF via src/lib/strategicReportPDF.js \u2014 downloadStrategicReportPDF({ subjects, playbook: true })\n4. The PDF includes: Cover page with S logo, Executive Summary, Individual Subject Reports (key findings, evidence chain, contact info, relatives, recommended actions, risk assessment, data quality), Data Verification and Methodology (30+ source categories), Strategic Pillars closing page\n\nBRAND IDENTITY: Logo = metallic 3D S in glowing blue ring. Colors = deep obsidian black #05070a, electric blue #00a8ff, cyan #00f2ff, white text. Tagline = INTELLIGENCE IN MOTION. Footer = AI STRATEGY, AUTOMATION, GROWTH, REAL RESULTS. Four pillars = Higher Visibility, More Qualified Traffic, Stronger Brand Authority, Real Business Growth. CTA = BUILD SMARTER. GROW FASTER.\n\nPROFESSIONAL RESEARCH STANDARDS (all covered by runMaxSkipTrace): Property ownership verification, court records search, professional license verification, social media intelligence, family network mapping, business affiliation discovery, public records aggregation, contact data verification, military records, genealogy archives, unclaimed property, newspaper archives, risk assessment, evidence chain documentation, data quality assessment, recommended next actions.\n\nREPORT TONE: Professional, objective, evidence-based. Never fabricate data. All claims backed by source citations. Use the StrategicReport page at /strategic-report to view and download reports."
  },
